# NON_AUTHORITATIVE — synthetic contract compatibility experiment

Detached P1a source proposal. Model records describe synthetic data only. Results do not grant authority, authorize promotion, certify actual independence or establish product behavior. No operational integration, registration, persistence, migration, dispatch, host adapter, credential or execution interface is provided.

Design basis: R3 and R4 of issue 37; inherited compatible R1/R2. Frozen parent 928d08edc691dfaeccd4929d2a6566d1f3a3a789, tree 5c3c6a5557b9faa7f7dfbb66d226afa38f17d4b4. Model domain FORGE_P1A_MODEL version 1 is distinct from historical operational versions. The original parser and projection are not imported or modified.

## Model surfaces

`validate_raw` handles strict raw ingress; `parse_record`, `canonical_bytes`, `digest`, and `record_ref` expose deterministic data transformations. `validate_record` and `validate_graph` inspect supplied primitive records and typed earlier references. `reduce_decision` returns a closed reducer result and separate snapshot; publication and staging are only in-memory descriptions. `evaluate_context`, `evaluate_command`, `evaluate_attempt`, `evaluate_evidence`, and `evaluate_acceptance` accept explicit independent fixture inputs. No API accepts a callable or selects a live resource. The JSON schema documents the closed record variants; lexical, canonical-order, graph, and policy constraints are checked in the model, not by a general JSON Schema engine.

Raw SHA-256 is separate from the full-envelope model digest. Canonical key order is Unicode scalar order, strings use literal UTF-8 except quotes, backslashes and lowercase control escapes, arrays retain order, and declared sets must already be strictly ordered by canonical element bytes. No normalization. Decision expiry and history use supplied ticks, not a clock. Logical operation keys survive lineage changes; only the attempt predecessor may cross lineage within the same repository. Independent expected controls are evaluated for exact applicability before verdict; a matching disconfirming control is a model match, not a product failure. Actual external fencing, one-winner concurrency and trust are outside this experiment.

## Public fixture custody and verification status

The `vectors.json` wrapper contains the exact original public-vector UTF-8 text, independently provided raw byte fixtures represented losslessly in hex, and original historical fixture bytes. The public-vector SHA-256 is c4cdbf36c9ded8ef8d54ef692c63ef4ef0dc454be7130859e59feb6656781ab3. Public archive SHA-256 is 9ad1d4814838301adee9713e784cacbdd32daef86af92f530c8d4ac9b7349642. Expected outcomes are not generated by the model. The test module maps all 47 raw and 76 semantic case IDs to explicit operations; the extra encoding-only example and historical byte custody checks are separate. No private cases included.

The source proposal is not an execution receipt. Historical V01–V05 measurements are separate calibration evidence; the new tests do not rerun the operational parser. V06–V15 are pending candidate execution, and V16 requires exact-parent diff and independent purity/isolation verification. No test results or production assurance are implied. The package is outside known fixed operational discovery roots; passive Markdown/Git scans may see it. Configurable roots, external consumers and active hosts are not qualified for this package. No actual runtime or deployment use is authorized by this descriptive artifact.

## Corrective R1 boundaries

New attempt proposals begin at local revision 1, independent of logical ordinal. Staged decision events must satisfy historical transitions at their own creation tick against their declared predecessor; valid stale orphans remain noncurrent. Mutable identity sharing across nested graph records and within auxiliary/history aggregates is rejected while independently decoded equal values are allowed. The input-graph validator remains strict. A structurally well-formed submitted evidence receipt with foreign or unresolved typed references is inapplicable and returns MODEL_UNKNOWN, not an applicable negative control; it cannot enter the graph. A submitted acceptance with foreign or unresolved evidence references likewise cannot qualify. Valid same-scope unrelated receipts remain excluded from applicable control credit; malformed records and graphs remain rejected. This distinction does not provide any authorization or live evidence.

Writer-authored R1 regressions are separate from the unchanged independent public oracle and use explicit expected statuses. The corrected source has not been executed in either normal or optimized mode; no independent successor acceptance is claimed.
